:"https://api.github.com/users/cornmonger/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cornmonger/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cornmonger/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cornmonger/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cornmonger/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"labeled","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2024-06-08T15:26:47Z","label":{"name":"type: bug","color":"B60205"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tauri-apps/tauri/issues/comments/2156176897","html_url":"https://github.com/tauri-apps/tauri/issues/10022#issuecomment-2156176897","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tauri-apps/tauri/issues/10022","id":2156176897,"node_id":"IC_kwDOC7lts86AhKYB","user":{"login":"roylaurie","id":281087,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4MTA4Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/281087?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roylaurie","html_url":"https://github.com/roylaurie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roylaurie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roylaurie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roylaurie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roylaurie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roylaurie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roylaurie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roylaurie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roylaurie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roylaurie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-06-08T20:44:27Z","updated_at":"2024-06-08T20:47:11Z","body":"This is a problem in `fontdb`, which is used by `resvg` (and `usvg`). There are actually two problems here:\r\n1. All fonts not working in text nodes. (solvable)\r\n2. Generic font families not working in text nodes. (requires a workaround)\r\n\r\nProblem 1 can be solved by bumping the version of the **resvg** dependency to 0.42.0, initializing a fontdb database object with `load_system_fonts()`, and then passing that to the existing `usvg` call.\r\n\r\nThis works for me by altering the `command` function in `tooling/cli/src/icon.rs` :\r\n```rust\r\nlet rtree = {\r\n        let mut fontdb = usvg::fontdb::Database::new();  //+\r\n        fontdb.load_system_fonts();  //+\r\n\r\n        let opt = usvg::Options {\r\n          // Get file's absolute directory.\r\n          resources_dir: std::fs::canonicalize(&input)\r\n            .ok()\r\n            .and_then(|p| p.parent().map(|p| p.to_path_buf())),\r\n            fontdb: Arc::new(fontdb),  //+\r\n            ..Default::default()\r\n        };\r\n\r\n        let svg_data = std::fs::read(&input).unwrap();\r\n        usvg::Tree::from_data(&svg_data, &opt).unwrap()  //*\r\n      };\r\n```\r\n\r\nProblem 2 is up to the `resvg` / `fontdb` team to solve permanently. A workaround would be to call the system's `fc-match` for the handful of generic family names (serif, sans-serif, cursive, fantasy, and monospace) and use the appropriate fontdb setters to pre-configure those, then pass it to `usvg`.\r\n\r\nHappy to submit a PR for this if needed.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tauri-apps/tauri/issues/comments/2156176897/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"roylaurie","id":281087,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4MTA4Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/281087?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roylaurie","html_url":"https://github.com/roylaurie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roylaurie/followers","fo